# Architecture Freeze — Phases 14–18

Phases **14–18** are feature-complete and **architecture-frozen** pending Live QA.

See `docs/ARCHITECTURE_FREEZE_PHASES_14_18.md`.

## Do not

- Redesign, replace, rename, or migrate business flows from Phases 14–18
- Change canonical workflows (publish → sell → invite → door → finance → analytics)
- Duplicate modules or invent parallel implementations (second check-in, finance, or analytics truth)
- Break backward compatibility of frozen APIs, routes, or data contracts
- Silently modify Phase 14–18 code to unblock Phases 19–25

## May

- Read frozen-phase data
- Reuse frozen-phase services
- Deep-link into frozen-phase UI
- Consume frozen-phase APIs

## If a later phase needs Phase 14–18 changes

1. Document the dependency and blast radius
2. Stop and ask for approval
3. Do not proceed with the change until approved

Regression fixes that restore documented Phase 14–18 behavior are OK. Rule/workflow changes are not.

Analytics remains read-only and must never invent metrics when canonical operational data exists.
